# The flight code's lint (unit 30): a MISRA-style subset, each check the mechanical form of a rule in
# CLAUDE.md beside this file. `cmake --build build/<preset> --target lint` runs it over the flight code
# (bus, osal, bc and every partition's logic); a finding fails the build. The mains, the stdin tools and the
# tests are not flight code and are not linted.
#
#   no recursion                          misc-no-recursion
#   no heap after initialisation          cppcoreguidelines-no-malloc, cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory
#   no unions or type punning on wire     cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-union-access, -pro-type-reinterpret-cast,
#   words, no casting away const          -pro-type-const-cast, -pro-type-cstyle-cast
#   explicit sizes and conversions        cppcoreguidelines-narrowing-conversions, hicpp-signed-bitwise,
#                                         google-explicit-constructor
#   every value initialised               cppcoreguidelines-init-variables, cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-member-init
#   every path of a decision written      hicpp-multiway-paths-covered, readability-braces-around-statements,
#                                         cppcoreguidelines-avoid-goto
#   a result that can fail is looked at   bugprone-unused-return-value, cert-err33-c
#   no doubles compared for equality,     cert-flp30-c, bugprone-* (the checks that find real mistakes: integer
#   and the usual traps                   division into a double, a widening after the overflow, a loop
#                                         counter too small for its bound, a suspicious sizeof, ...)
#
# Left out, with the reason:
#   bugprone-branch-clone                 every partition's state rule reads INITIALIZING-and-fresh -> NORMAL,
#                                         NORMAL-and-stale -> DEGRADED, DEGRADED-and-fresh -> NORMAL: two branches
#                                         with one body, written out because that is the rule
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters  a style opinion about (rt, sa) and (row, column), not a defect
#   bugprone-exception-escape             the flight code is built with -fno-exceptions
# osal/.clang-tidy leaves out one more for the operating system layer.
#
# To drop a check for one line, say why on that line: // NOLINT(check-name): reason
Checks: >
  -*,
  misc-no-recursion,
  cppcoreguidelines-no-malloc,
  cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-union-access,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-const-cast,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-cstyle-cast,
  cppcoreguidelines-narrowing-conversions,
  cppcoreguidelines-init-variables,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-member-init,
  cppcoreguidelines-avoid-goto,
  hicpp-signed-bitwise,
  hicpp-multiway-paths-covered,
  google-explicit-constructor,
  readability-braces-around-statements,
  cert-err33-c,
  cert-flp30-c,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-branch-clone,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-exception-escape
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*[/\\](bus|osal|bc|partitions)[/\\](include|[a-z_]+[/\\]include)[/\\].*'
CheckOptions:
  - key: hicpp-signed-bitwise.IgnorePositiveIntegerLiterals
    value: true
  - key: hicpp-multiway-paths-covered.WarnOnMissingElse
    value: false
  - key: cppcoreguidelines-narrowing-conversions.PedanticMode
    value: false
